: fixture: anthropic-messages/03-parallel-tools.sse
: protocol: Anthropic Messages API, streaming, two client tool calls in one assistant turn (parallel tool use)
: provenance: CONSTRUCTED by R2 from the documented schema. Parallel tool use = several tool_use content blocks in one
:   assistant message (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/parallel-tool-use, checked 2026-11-11);
:   event framing from https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming (checked 2026-11-11).
: note: the docs say each block's index matches its position in the final content array. Whether two tool_use blocks can
:   be interleaved (block 2 deltas before block 1 stop) is NOT documented; this fixture keeps them sequential. The adapter
:   must still key accumulation by index, not by "current block".
: note: the usage cache fields in message_start are constructed values in the documented field names.
: expected ModelEvents: ToolCallReady(toolu_01AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA, get_weather, {"location":"Taipei"}),
:   ToolCallReady(toolu_01BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB, get_time, {"timezone":"Asia/Taipei"}), Usage, Completed(stop=tool_use).
:   Both results must later be sent back in ONE user message, tool_result blocks first.

